Gemma 4 and Ollama
================================================================================

Gemma 4 E4B (the default local LLM: ILANG_PIZZA_LLM=gemma4:e4b)
  By Google DeepMind. Pulled by the user with `ollama pull gemma4:e4b` and run
  on the user's machine; not redistributed here.
  License: Apache License 2.0
  https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/gemma_4_license
  Model card: https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-E4B-it
  Earlier generations (Gemma 1, 2 and 3) were released under the separate
  Gemma Terms of Use (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms). If you point
  ILANG_PIZZA_LLM at one of them, those terms apply instead.

Ollama (local model server, installed separately by the user)
  License: MIT. https://github.com/ollama/ollama
  The ollama Python client is also MIT: https://github.com/ollama/ollama-python


================================================================================
Data sources
================================================================================

Open-Meteo (optional rain lookup for event days)
  Weather data by Open-Meteo.com (https://open-meteo.com/)
  API data are offered under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (CC BY 4.0): https://open-meteo.com/en/licence
  The free API is for non-commercial use only and is rate limited:
  https://open-meteo.com/en/terms
  Requests carry only a venue's coordinates and dates, never attendee data.
  Turn the lookup off with --no-weather.

Philippine holidays
  From the holidays package (MIT): https://github.com/vacanza/holidays

PAGASA (optional weather.csv supplied by the organizer)
  Data obtained from PAGASA comes with PAGASA's own terms of use. Keep it in
  data/ (gitignored) unless those terms allow sharing.


